PE 911: Khinchin's Constant / 辛钦常数

=== Problem Overview ===
Khinchin's constant K0 is the almost-everywhere limit of
the geometric mean of continued fraction coefficients.

K0 = prod_{r=1}^{∞} (1 + 1/(r(r+2)))^{log2(r)} ≈ 2.685452...

This problem defines a variant: for randomly chosen (a,b),
consider the continued fraction expansion of a/b and examine
the distribution of coefficients under a modified weighting.

s_k = first index m where a_m ≥ k (in the CF of a/b)
The limit involves weighed sums over these s_k values.

=== Key Concepts ===
  1. Gauss-Kuzmin distribution: P(a_m = k) ≈ -log2(1 - 1/(k+1)^2)
  2. Modified distributions for correlated coefficients
  3. Numerical estimation of infinite products/sums
  4. High-precision floating point arithmetic

=== PE Answer ===
  5679.934966
